    "url": "https://www.uni-wuerzburg.de/en/equity/family-service-centre/information/financial-benefits/",
    "title": "Financial benefits -",
    "text": "Financial benefits - Deutsch Intern Stop animation Family service Here you will find an overview of the financial benefits and funding opportunities. Parental allowance, parental allowance plus, partnership bonus... There are many options. The Federal Ministry for Family Affairs, Senior Citizens, Women and Youth can provide you with more detailed information. The parental allowance calculator and planner can help you plan the parental allowance months and the different  combinations of parental allowance, parental allowance plus and partnership bonus. Your local advice and information center in Lower Franconia is the Zentrum Bayern Familie und Soziales . The easy online application for parental allowance is available online. Child benefits are one of the most important benefits for families in Germany. You can find a detailed description of this family benefit on the website of the Federal Ministry for Family Affairs, Senior Citizens, Women and Youth . The application for child benefits can be submitted to the Office of Family Benefits. You can find out which family benefits office is responsible for you, as well as the online child benefit application form on the Family and Children page of the Federal Employment Agency . The Free State of Bavaria also supports parents whose children are between the ages of 13 and 36 months with a monthly amount of 250 euros, and this amount increases up to 300 euros per month beginning with the third child.If you have applied for parental allowance in Bavaria and it has been approved, this application  will also count as an application for the Bavarian family allowance. Further information on family allowance can be found on the website of the Zentrum Bayern Familie & Soziales . The state foundation \"Hilfe für Mutter und Kind\" can provide supplementary benefits for pregnant women and mothers in emergency situations if, in individual cases, the standard social programs such as child benefits and parental allowance are not sufficient enough to cover costs. Expectant mothers must apply before the birth of the child, otherwise it is not possible to apply for this type of support. In Würzburg, the application can be submitted to state-approved advice centers for pregnancy issues: Protestant Counseling Center - Pregnancy & Sexuality Catholic counseling center for pregnancy issues at SkF State-approved advice center for pregnancy issues at the Würzburg District Office Pro Familia Würzburg Applications to this fund can be submitted before the start of maternity leave by the facultyvia the respective faculty management, which should check and confirm the appropriateness of the requested measure to Department 4 - Human Resources Service Center. This department will then examine more favorable solutions in terms of personnel and financesduring a consultation and only then implement the requested measures at the expense of its own funds, which will be designated in advance by the faculties. After one year, the fund's resources will be distributed to the faculties on a pro rata basis for refinancing within the set budget cap. Only completed cases are taken into account; cases spanning more than one year are reimbursed in full in the following year. Applications to this fund can be submitted informally to ”Unit 3.1 – Budget Department“ before the start of the trip. The prerequisite is a conference or congress trip by academic staff who have to take a child up to the age of 3 with them on the trip. Female academics are eligible to apply directly. At the end of the trip, the additional costs incurred in connection with traveling with the infant (e.g. also for an accompanying person) will be reimbursed on the basis of the regulations of the Bavarian travel expenses law. The relevant original receipts, certificates, invoices, etc. must be submitted to “Unit 3.1“ Contact Familienservice Campus Hubland Nord Klara-Oppenheimer-Weg 38 97074 Würzburg Phone: +49 931 31-84342 Email Find Contact Hubland Nord, Gebäude 38 Home The University Studying at JMU Research Teaching Institutions International The University Dates and Deadlines Degree Programmes and Subjects News Jobs at JMU Staff Members Glossary of Administrative Terms Official publications Services University Library IT Services University Sport Academic Advisory Service Examination Office Student Affairs Student Representation Career Centre Your JMU WueStudy WueCampus Class Schedule Online Enrolment Library Catalogue Contact Phone and Address Directory How to Find Us Press Academic Advisory Service Störungsannahme Technical Maintenance Service Need help quickly? Page options Sitemap Picture credits To top Last update: 28.10.2025 Page: 208642/356 Picture credits Imprint + Privacy Policy Privacy Disclaimer Barrierefreiheit",
    "date": null,
    "scraped_at": "2026-07-12T19:50:19.251428",
    "source": "web"
  },
